    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** leading the way at a 78.62, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Keller. His elite sprint speed\u2014our primary offensive filter\u2014combined with a #3 hole assignment and a soft SP_xERA of 4.26 makes him our clear anchor. **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) also project as high-end starts; **James Wood** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill matchup against Woods Richardson, while **Mickey Moniak** gains significant ground due to the park factors in his favor and a prominent #2 spot in the lineup. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a set-and-forget play at 72.92, bolstered by a strong platoon advantage against Cecconi.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Jose Caballero**. While his raw metrics suggest he could contribute if inserted, his current status as a non-starter mandates a floor of 0.0 to protect our total game caps. We are also navigating a light day for our bench depth, with **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang** on team off-days, and **Seiya Suzuki** sidelined, leaving us unable to leverage their production. Meanwhile, **Trevor Story** remains a high-risk start at 52.39; despite his favorable 100% SB potential against the slow delivery of Jax, his score is severely hampered by a -19% SP skill penalty against a legitimate arm, making him a marginal play despite the stolen base upside.\n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely, though our primary focus remains the consistency of **Tyler Soderstrom** (63.50) and **Travis Bazzana** (56.70). **Tyler Soderstrom** is primed for a productive day in the #3 spot, and we expect **Travis Bazzana** to provide just enough stability to justify his start despite a tougher matchup against Lugo. As we continue to manage the roster\u2014including the status of **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Luis Campusano**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young**\u2014our objective remains maximizing daily efficiency scores while aggressively chasing SB volume where the matchups allow.",
